<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boris of Tver</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–1461</span> · Also known as Boris Alexandrovich of Tver</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boris Alexandrovich was Grand Prince of Tver from 1425 to 1461. He restored Tver's strength as an independent power between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, allying first with Vytautas of Lithuania and later with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow">Vasily II of Moscow</a> during the Muscovite civil war, and his court produced chronicles and other writings praising his rule. His son Mikhail Borisovich was Tver's last grand prince.</p></div>
